---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const pageTitle = "Privacy Policy";
const lastUpdated = "11 November 2026";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <section class="cnf-section">
    <div class="cnf-privacy">
      <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</em></p>

      <p>
        This policy explains what personal data Club na Fealsúnachta
        ("we", "us") collects through clubnafealsunachta.com, why we
        collect it, and what rights you have over it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Club na Fealsúnachta is run by
        Francis Quinn, based in Trieste, Italy. For any
        question about this policy or your data, contact
        <a href="mailto:info@clubnafealsunachta.com">info@clubnafealsunachta.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Member account:</strong> if you join the club through the
          site, we store your username, email address, a hashed (never
          plain-text) password, when you joined, and when your email address
          was confirmed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Profile:</strong> you can add your full name and a profile
          photo. Your profile page publicly shows your username, photo, the
          month you joined and the chapters you're in; your full name is only
          shown publicly if you choose to show it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>RSVPs:</strong> if you RSVP to an event (going, maybe or
          not going), we store your answer. Other logged-in members can see
          your name and photo in that event's lists, and your profile page
          publicly shows how many past events you said you were going to.
          Creating an event marks you as going to it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Posts and events:</strong> anything you publish on the site,
          such as a post or an event, is public and shows your name as the
          author.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Chapters:</strong> if you join a chapter, we store that
          you're a member and whether you asked for emails about its
          upcoming events. Those emails are off unless you tick the box when
          joining, and you can switch them off or leave the chapter any time
          in your profile settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact form:</strong> if you message us, your name, email,
          and message are sent to our inbox by email. We do not store this
          in a database.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Topic suggestions:</strong> only members can suggest topics,
          for a chapter they're in. The topics and the chapter are sent to our
          inbox by email. Your name is only included if you choose to add it,
          and then it's the name you show on your profile; otherwise the
          suggestion just says it came from a member of that chapter.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Newsletter:</strong> if you subscribe, your email address
          is sent to our mailing list provider, Mailchimp, who handles
          delivery and unsubscribes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Login session:</strong> when you log in, we set cookies in
          your browser so you stay signed in (see Cookies below). They are not
          used for tracking or advertising.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>
        We use this data only to run the club: to create and secure your
        member account, to reply to messages sent through the contact
        form, to read topic suggestions, to send the newsletter to people who asked for it, to email
        chapter members who asked about upcoming events, and to show your
        profile, RSVPs and posts to other members and visitors. We do
        not sell or share your data for advertising purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We use a small number of external services to run the site, each
        of which processes data on our behalf:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Supabase</strong> — hosts our database and profile photos,
          including member accounts (data region: West EU (Ireland)).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Mailchimp</strong> (United States) — manages newsletter
          delivery and subscriptions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zoho</strong> (EU) — ZeptoMail sends our emails: contact
          and topic suggestion messages, account emails such as email
          confirmation and password resets, and chapter event emails. Zoho
          Mail hosts our inbox, where contact and topic suggestion messages
          are kept.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Netlify</strong> (United States) — hosts the site and
          processes server logs, which include IP addresses, for every
          request.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Member accounts are kept until you delete your account. If you
        start creating an account but never confirm your email address, that
        unconfirmed signup is automatically deleted after about 30 days.
        Newsletter addresses are kept until you unsubscribe. Contact form
        and topic suggestion messages aren't stored in a database, but the
        email itself remains in our inbox until we delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under GDPR, you have the right to access, correct, delete, or
        export your personal data, and to withdraw consent (e.g.
        unsubscribe from the newsletter) at any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can change your username, full name, photo, email address and
        password, and delete your account, yourself in your profile settings.
        Deleting your account removes your account, profile photo, chapter
        memberships, any chapter admin rights, and RSVPs. Posts and events
        you published stay on the site, credited to "Former member" instead
        of your name. A newsletter subscription is separate: unsubscribe from
        any newsletter email.
      </p>
      <p>
        For anything else, such as a copy of your data or removing your
        profile photo, email
        <a href="mailto:info@clubnafealsunachta.com">info@clubnafealsunachta.com</a>
        and we'll handle your request directly.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data
        protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We only use strictly necessary cookies, all set when you log in: one
        keeps you signed in, and two small ones let pages show your account
        menu and profile photo straight away. Your browser also keeps a copy
        of your username, name and photo for the same reason. We don't use
        analytics or advertising cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the site changes. The "last updated"
        date above will always reflect the latest version.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
